{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04YK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X}' \\subset \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$f(\\mathcal{X}')$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0ab4f6f73f4d3171b4bedaf7ce9ff80785fa765c0345a49da9a4d688afb256a2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:284294f14e07a68bcccfd0ce3e3bd8b634bfb2259b023cdc9d0f23f052b740df", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis definition should be used with caution. Namely, if\n<MATH_0001> is an equivalence of algebraic stacks\nand <MATH_0002> is an open substack, then it\nis not necessarily the case that the subcategory <MATH_0003>\nis an open substack of <MATH_0004>. The problem is that it may not\nbe a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>strictly<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> full subcategory; but this is also the only problem.\nHere is a formal statement.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bd3c908ce01cd0cf696fd59aa223705c39271a490fe92ed005955f5196d09085", "unit_id": "tag:04YK:prose-0005"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04YK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$i : \\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X}' \\subset \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$i$", "MATH_0004": "$i' : \\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{X}'$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{X}' \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0006": "$i$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{X}'$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-substack-image}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1759fedfcedf274c52d517d3f0fa07e37fea3c63911eb981e800bbf5004eceba", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a88d9bf3b0f3d3cecdf915c5218bfb8ebd118d8763d4e0679a9fc93700394942", "source_text": "For any immersion <MATH_0001> there exists a\nunique locally closed substack <MATH_0002>\nsuch that <MATH_0003> factors as the composition of\nan equivalence <MATH_0004>\nfollowed by the inclusion morphism <MATH_0005>.\nIf <MATH_0006> is a closed (resp.<SPACE_0001>open) immersion, then <MATH_0007>\nis a closed (resp.<SPACE_0002>open) substack of <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0148807b17707663b82d3901f125e9157eb466efbe550fdc135d4f951004d418", "unit_id": "tag:0506:statement"}
